# Update README and docs on every user-facing change

User documentation is the wiki: `docs/` (English, canonical) and `docs/pt-BR/` (page-for-page mirror). Do not treat `docs/superpowers/` as user docs.

Before considering work complete, map whether the change affects public API, packages, CLI, examples, HTTP behavior, message catalogs, or install steps.

## What to update

- `README.md` — install, packages, example, compatibility, links
- The matching page in `docs/`
- The same filename in `docs/pt-BR/` in the same change
- `docs/api-reference.md` and `docs/pt-BR/api-reference.md` when public API or XML docs change

If a user-facing change lands without those updates, the work is not done.

## Skip (do not force cosmetic README diffs)

- Internal refactors with no contract or behavior change
- Tests, CI, formatting
- `docs/superpowers/` (historical)

```text
❌ Changed ToHttpResult and committed only C#
✅ Same change updates docs/aspnet-guide.md, docs/pt-BR/aspnet-guide.md,
   and the README example when the public contract or sample changed
```
